Join Axon and be a Force for Good.

At Axon, we’re on a mission to Protect Life. We’re explorers, pursuing society’s most critical safety and justice issues with our ecosystem of devices and cloud software. Like our products, we work better together. We connect with candor and care, seeking out diverse perspectives from our customers, communities and each other.

Life at Axon is fast-paced, challenging and meaningful. Here, you’ll take ownership and drive real change. Constantly grow as you work hard for a mission that matters at a company where you matter.

Your Impact &nbsp;

Are you a privacy attorney who thrives at the intersection of emerging technology and global regulation? Do you have a passion for helping innovative teams build responsibly, while navigating complex privacy and AI challenges with clarity and precision? Do you bring a global mindset, a practical problem-solving approach, and a collaborative spirit to everything you do?&nbsp;

Axon is looking for its second ever dedicated Privacy &amp; AI Counsel to join our Legal team, reporting to our VP of Legal Product &amp; Innovation.&nbsp;

In this role, you’ll partner closely with product, AI, and employment teams to embed privacy and ethical AI into the core of Axon’s products and operations. From body-worn cameras and SaaS platforms to machine learning models and global privacy frameworks, you’ll play a critical role in answering complex questions in highly regulated markets around the world. Your guidance will help shape how Axon responsibly builds the future of public safety and justice technology.&nbsp;

What You'll Do &nbsp;

Location: Boston, MA, NYC, NY, Atlanta, GA, or Sterling, VA required to be in-office 4x week (Tuesday - Friday)&nbsp;

Partner across teams to support privacy and AI compliance in Axon’s products, global operations, and culture-through scalable guidance and hands-on execution.&nbsp;

Counsel on ethical and legal considerations of obtaining, handling, and using AI training data and outputs. Identify opportunities for and implement AI-augmented workflows, skills, and agents in the team’s work.

Drive implementation of privacy principles across products and internal operations by advising on and owning key workflows: impact assessments, DSARs, DPAs, and third-party/sub-processor reviews.&nbsp;

Work closely with Axon’s existing privacy counsel to build, refine, and implement privacy and AI processes.&nbsp;

Exercise sound judgment and strong self-direction within a fast-growing, global business.&nbsp;

Partner closely with relevant stakeholders to provide guidance during and after incident response and remediation. &nbsp;

What You Bring &nbsp;

JD , admission to and in good standing with at least one US state bar.&nbsp;

Minimum of 3 years of experience practicing privacy or data protection law, ideally advising on technology, SaaS businesses, or AI-related products in highly regulated industries.&nbsp;

Experience advising on privacy regulations globally (e.g., GDPR, US state privacy laws, PIPEDA, Australia’s Privacy Act, LGPD).&nbsp;

Expertise advising on and implementing enterprise privacy via cross-border transfer mechanisms, intra-group data transfer agreements, and DPA drafting and review.&nbsp;

Ability to navigate ambiguity, distill complexity, and work collaboratively across teams while always upholding Axon’s Win Right value.&nbsp;

Fluency and comfort applying AI tools, prompts, and agents to accelerate and improve operations.

Strong communication skills and a practical, solution-oriented mindset.&nbsp;

Privacy certifications such as CIPP/US, CIPP/E, or CIPT are a plus.&nbsp;

Other pluses: regional expertise with the EU or experience in the healthcare industry.&nbsp;

Benefits that Benefit You

• Competitive salary and 401k with employer match

• Discretionary paid time off

• Paid parental leave for all

• Medical, Dental, Vision plans

• Fitness Programs

• Emotional &amp; Mental Wellness support

• Learning &amp; Develo

Category: IT Services

Location:

For an international organization in New York, we are urgently looking for a Full Remote Senior API Developer - Azure. As Full Remote Senior API Developer, you are responsible for the design, creation, and delivery of a range of supporting APIs and Azure platform elements to support the implementation of a central API system for data synchronization/exchange between data platforms in a hub and spoke architecture model.

Candidates need to be able to work 4/5 hours per day in the normal office hours of New York, US. Example 9AM NY time equals 7:30PM. This role is open for employees and contractors

Tasks and responsibilities:

• Analyze, design, develop, as well as implement RESTful services and APIs;

• Be involved in the development life cycle and perform definition and feasibility analysis;

• Implement, integrate, and document a variety of software platforms through the REST API framework;

• Apply the latest software design techniques and contribute to the technical design of new solutions;

• Modify existing programs, prepare test data and functional specifications;

• Troubleshoot issues and solve problems, identify potential process improvement areas;

• Implement common APIs based on architecture guidelines and frameworks;

• Write object-oriented, clean, and maintainable code;

• Deliver quality results on time with minimal supervision;

Profile:

​

• Bachelor or Master degree;

• +2 years of experience in a computing environment with multiple programming languages (Python, Java, JavaScript, Node.js etc.);

• +1 year of experience with Azure Cloud portal;

• Proficiency in working with Azure Data Factory, Azure Data Lake is required;

• Familiarity with code versioning tools, like Git, SVN, and Mercurial is required;

• Experience in creating REST API documentation using Swagger and YAML or similar tools is desirable;

• Experience with Azure DevOps and Azure Purview is a plus;

• Any professional certifications encouraged;

• Fluent in English;

